0027:     """
0028:     Erase every pixel whose color matches the marker inside the corner bracket, except for the marker itself.
0029: 
0030:     Input structure
0031:     - The background is the most common color.
0032:     - There is exactly one monochromatic 4-connected corner bracket object.
0033:     - Inside the bracket bbox, outside the bracket cells, there is exactly one foreground marker pixel.
0034:     Rule
0035:     - Read the marker color.
0036:     - Recolor every other pixel of that color to the background.
0037:     - Leave the bracket, the marker, and all other colors unchanged.
0038:     Key insight
0039:     - The bracket is a color selector: its enclosed marker names the color to delete everywhere else.
0040:     """
